From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode-port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:22:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D509 code mode: Object.prototype.toString names Math, JSON
 and console

Upstream: Math, JSON and console were plain data objects, so Object.prototype.toString.call(Math) (and String(Math)) gave "[object Object]" instead of "[object Math]", "[object JSON]" and "[object console]", although interpreter-support.md says toString reports every built-in kind as JS does through Symbol.toStringTag.
Fixed: the three namespaces are a namespace object kind that carries its tag. Diagnostics still call them "a data object". Both engines; the VM snapshot saves the tag and restores an unchanged namespace by name.
Scenarios: codemode-stdlib-numeric.test.ts "math" (Math props), codemode-stdlib-object.test.ts "json parse and stringify" (JSON tag) and "object statics" (toString tags), codemode-stdlib-console.test.ts "console formatting" (tag)
Upstream tests: test/stdlib.test.ts adds "names the Math, JSON, and console namespaces, which stay plain data in diagnostics"

